"""Readable evidence for the source pilot and matched transcript-history checks."""
from html import escape as e
import json
from pathlib import Path
from build_question_overview import document,table,clock,p
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=ROOT/'research/question-study'
def read(name):return json.loads((D/name).read_text())
def main():
 source=read('source-review.json');reader=read('reader-review.json');teacher=read('teacher-curation.json');resources=read('resources.json');controls=read('silence-controls.json')['controls'];names={'full':'Full transcript with speakers','recent60':'Segments released in the last 60 seconds','no_speakers':'Full transcript without speaker fields','state_plus_new':'Automatic notes plus speech since the last update'};grades={'complete':'Complete answer','partial':'Incomplete or unsupported additions','incorrect':'Wrong main answer','no_answer':'No earlier answer recovered'}
 body='<header class="hero"><span class="eyebrow">Steps 1–2 · completed text diagnostics</span><h1>Source review and history checks</h1><p class="lede">The full transcript supports useful answers, but the first automatic note cache loses too much information. Qwen3-30B Instruct gives 13 complete answers out of the frozen 20 with full history, compared with four using the initial notes plus new speech.</p><p>The note cache is the limited private note list supplied instead of the full older transcript. These are source-based judgments by Codex on a small selected pilot. They are not independent human ratings or a streaming speech-system result. <a href="question-plan.html">Return to the project TODO and proposed when/what-to-think experiments.</a></p></header>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="dataset"><h2>What step 1 now contains</h2><p>The original twenty question IDs and their existing recordings stay frozen across six meetings, with no participant overlap with the five earlier F5-development meetings. AMI’s A–D letters identify speakers within a meeting. Codex checked the required answer facts, uncertainty limits and plausible requester motivation against earlier source speech. Extra examples in an old reference answer are optional unless the question actually asks for them.</p>'+table(1,'The pilot and its controls. Four text probes are separate from the twenty original questions and do not increase the existing 105-question audio-bank count.',['Item','Count','What was checked'],[['Frozen recorded questions','20 / 6 meetings','Source support, current decision status, requester motivation and existing audio evidence.'],['Targeted text probes','4','Two responsibility checks, a follow-up commitment and a changed proposal. These have no new synthesized audio.'],['Ordinary-discussion controls','6 / 108 s','Unmodified source audio with no Assistant wake cue; expected outward action is to listen.'],['Participant overlap with earlier audio development','0','Official AMI global participant IDs checked across the meeting split.']])+'<p>The twenty mostly test rules, constraints and decisions. Some are delayed reminders of the requester’s own earlier statements; these are plausible but less compelling than a new task dependency. The four probes expose responsibility and revision errors without rewriting the frozen set. This is still too small and selected to certify a general multi-hop benchmark.</p><p><strong>Checks reused:</strong> all twenty processed questions have Parakeet’s Assistant-first result; sixteen match the full question after case, punctuation, common number and contraction normalization, and eighteen after declared spelling/acronym equivalence. Whisper recognizes the cue first in nineteen. Every conditioning clip is earlier speech. The minimum recorded speaker-similarity score (ECAPA cosine, where higher means more similar recordings) is '+f"{source['audio_checks_reused']['minimum_ECAPA_cosine']:.3f}"+'. These are automatic diagnostics, not proof of perceived identity or naturalness. No TTS or ASR job was rerun for this review.</p><p><strong>Simplification:</strong> Codex’s documented source/motivation review and the existing audio checks are sufficient for this operational pilot. Independent human listening and naturalness ratings remain optional and uncollected; they are not marked as completed.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="reader"><h2>What history lets the reader answer</h2><p>One fixed Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 model ran through vLLM. Each question was tested with the same requester and text under four conditions. The reader never received the reference facts or selected answer evidence. The note writer received past speech and its own earlier notes; it was never given the test questions. “Recent” means complete transcript segments whose assumed release time falls in the last sixty seconds. Release time is the manual segment end plus 0.5 seconds; it is not measured ASR latency.</p><ul>'+''.join('<li><strong>'+e(names[k])+'.</strong> '+e(v)+'</li>' for k,v in reader['conditions'].items())+'</ul><p>The no-speaker condition removes speaker fields, while retaining the same words, times and passage IDs. Names actually spoken in the meeting remain. The note condition uses question-blind updates every two source minutes, retaining up to 32 active records, plus all speech since its last checkpoint. Its recent span differs from the last-minute control, so this is a storage diagnostic rather than a fair timing experiment.</p><p>Codex used these criteria for every captured response:</p><ul>'+''.join('<li><strong>'+e(grades[k])+':</strong> '+e(v)+'</li>' for k,v in reader['grade_definitions'].items())+'</ul>'
 def results(cohort):return [[names[r['condition']],r['n'],r['complete'],r['partial'],r['incorrect'],r['no_answer']] for r in reader['summaries'] if r['cohort']==cohort]
 body+=table(2,'Outcomes for the same twenty frozen questions. Each row sums to twenty; source-based judgments use the definitions above. A no-answer result is often appropriate caution when the supplied history omits the fact.',['History supplied','Questions','Complete answer','Incomplete / unsupported additions','Wrong main answer','No earlier answer recovered'],results('frozen20'))
 body+=table(3,'Four additional text diagnostics, reported separately. These are case studies, not a new accuracy benchmark.',['History supplied','Probes','Complete answer','Incomplete / unsupported additions','Wrong main answer','No earlier answer recovered'],results('text_diagnostic4'))
 body+='<p>All 96 responses completed their structured output; none cited an unknown passage outside its supplied material. That did not prevent wrong answers. Five of the twenty note-condition answers cited supplied internal note IDs instead of the requested original passage IDs. Those aliases can be mapped back to their sources, but the caller must do that explicitly.</p><p><strong>Interpretation:</strong> the full history helps recover older information, but a stronger reader still invents certainty and confuses quantities. Removing speaker fields often leaves enough content for these mostly factual reminders; this does not establish that speaker tracking is unnecessary. The targeted responsibility probes reveal mistakes that the main set underrepresents.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="examples"><h2>What the errors mean in context</h2><article class="catalog-question"><h3>A total-profit goal is not a per-unit margin</h3><p>In ES2006a, C gives a €25 selling price, a €12.50 production-cost ceiling and a separate €50 million total-profit target. With full transcript history, the reader answers that the exact profit margin is €50 million. The source instead permits a conditional €12.50 per-unit surplus, 50% of the selling price, before unspecified other costs. A fluent answer and valid source IDs do not resolve this difference.</p></article><article class="catalog-question"><h3>The person speaking is not automatically the requester</h3><p>In TS3006c, A says they must record decisions in the final report. The no-speaker reader assigns that statement to requester B. The note condition names A and B even though its second cited acknowledgement is spoken by D. In another probe, the spoken introduction “my name is Maarika” survives removal of speaker fields, so the reader can still recover that person’s interface-design role. A speaker-field ablation is not the same as erasing every identity clue.</p></article><article class="catalog-question"><h3>A rule can disappear before the question arrives</h3><p>The EN2004a source tells annotators to choose one interpretation when two are equally plausible. The note writer never selects that rule. For the scrollwheel location in TS3004d, it does propose a useful left-side note, but changes the source quotation and fails the exact-quote check. These are different failures: choosing the wrong work versus losing a useful fact during note construction.</p></article></section>'
 guard=reader['note_guard'];body+='<section class="section" id="state"><h2>The first meeting-state prototype needs repair</h2><p>The model produced 410 proposed note changes during 67 updates. Code checked that every quoted substring appeared in its cited, already available source and that a claimed speaker had cited speech. It retained 299 changes and left 111 unused: 110 had a quotation mismatch and three had unsupported speaker fields, with two changes having both kinds of problem. A quotation mismatch can be a changed capital letter or cleaned-up disfluency; it does not mean every rejected claim was factually false.</p>'+table(4,'What the automatic provenance guard checked. Counts concern proposed note changes, not questions, model calls or proven factual errors.',['Object','Count','Meaning'],[['Proposed note changes','410','Up to eight changes per model update.'],['Changes retained by the guard','299','Passed source-ID, literal quotation and basic speaker checks; claim meaning is still not certified.'],['Changes left unused','111','Failed at least one check; the old notes were preserved.'],['Maximum active records in each supplied snapshot','32','A simple chronological cap, not a learned relevance or durable-memory policy.']])+'<p>Even surviving notes can attach the wrong person to a claim, upgrade a suggestion into an agreement, or omit a price needed for a calculation. The current cache yields only four complete answers out of twenty. This is evidence against treating the first compact cache as ready; it is not evidence that structured memory can never help.</p><p>Before the speech comparison, the proposed repair is to copy source text by code, separate who spoke from who owns a task, preserve durable facts until they are contradicted, and check a claim’s meaning rather than only its quotation. These repairs are explicit gates in step 3, not unreported improvements to this captured run.</p><p><a href="../research/question-study/state-snapshots.json">All captured draft state snapshots</a> · <a href="../research/question-study/prompt-templates.json">Actual prompt templates and limits</a></p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="teacher"><h2>Earlier teacher traces are kept out of training</h2><p>The original 64 free-form teacher outputs all reached the generation cap without a complete note object. Ten later completion outputs had already received a content audit that found shifted quotations, stale updates, uncertainty loss and some note items with no proposition text. Completing a response did not make the whole trace reliable.</p>'+table(5,'Simplified curation outcome. Whole outputs are quarantined; the small development fact records are not private reasoning traces and are not a training run.',['Material','Count','Use'],[['Original unfinished teacher outputs','64','Preserved for diagnosis; excluded as whole training targets.'],['Later completion outputs','10','Existing content audit reused; excluded as whole training targets.'],['Source-checked structured development records','5','Owner, fact/status, source/time and one explicit deadline update; candidates for later development only.'],['Evaluation cases used for training','0','The six evaluation meetings remain excluded.']])+'<p>For example, A first volunteers to prepare the call for titles/abstracts, then adds an end-of-week deadline. The curated update preserves A as the owner and adds the deadline without inventing a calendar date. Another record keeps “probably about thirty” as an estimate of names on a postgraduate list, rather than a count of confirmed talks.</p><p><a href="../research/question-study/teacher-curation.json">Exclusion manifest, prior findings and five source-checked records</a></p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="silence"><h2>Ordinary discussion: listen without speaking</h2><p>These six 18-second excerpts contain original participant discussion, with no synthetic question or Assistant wake cue. Under the experiment’s addressing rule, the expected outward action is to listen. Private preparation is allowed. This does not label every ordinary meeting moment as forbidding all possible proactive assistance, and no duplex model has yet been tested on these controls.</p>'
 for c in controls:body+='<article class="catalog-question"><h3>'+e(c['meeting']+' · '+clock(c['start'])+'–'+clock(c['end']))+'</h3><audio controls preload="none" aria-label="Ordinary discussion '+c['meeting']+'" src="../research/question-study/'+c['path']+'"></audio><details><summary>Words fully contained in this excerpt</summary>'+p(' '.join(w['text'] for w in c['transcript_words']))+'</details></article>'
 body+='</section><section class="section" id="inspect"><h2>Inspect each question, source and reader response</h2><p>The first twenty are the original frozen questions. The four text probes are clearly marked. References below are source-checking labels for review, never inputs to the note writer or reader.</p>'
 for q in source['questions']:
  slug=q['id'].replace(':','--');body+='<details class="catalog-question" id="review-'+slug+'"><summary>'+e(q['meeting']+' · '+clock(q['at'])+' · '+('Frozen question' if q['cohort']=='frozen20' else 'Separate text probe'))+'</summary><p class="question">'+e(q['question'])+'</p>'+p(q['motivation_review'])+'<h3>Required answer facts</h3><ul>'+''.join('<li>'+e(x)+'</li>' for x in q['required_facts'])+'</ul><h3>Source speech before the request</h3>'
  for s in q['source_evidence']:body+='<p><strong>'+e(s['speaker']+' · '+clock(s['start'])+'–'+clock(s['end']))+'</strong> '+e(s['text'])+' <small>('+e(s['id'])+')</small></p>'
  for r in [r for r in reader['decisions'] if r['id']==q['id']]:body+='<article class="catalog-question"><h3>'+e(names[r['condition']])+'</h3><p><strong>'+e(grades[r['grade']])+'.</strong> '+e(r['reason'])+'</p><p><strong>Captured reader answer:</strong> '+e(r['answer'])+'</p>'+p('Cited IDs: '+(', '.join(r['evidence_ids']) or 'none'))+'</article>'
  if q['cohort']=='frozen20':body+='<p><a href="question-audio.html#'+slug+'">Listen to the existing question recording</a></p>'
  body+='</details>'
 body+='</section><footer class="section"><h2>Resources and reproducibility</h2>'+table(6,'The only new GPU job in this study. Source review, extraction, token-budget checks, curation and webpage work use zero GPUs.',['Job','GPU count / type / VRAM','GPU role','Dependencies and sharing','Allocation'],[[resources['job'],'1 × A100-SXM4 80 GB','Qwen3-30B Instruct weights and KV cache on GPU 0','One vLLM engine; note updates followed by reader conditions; no S1, ASR or speech service alongside it.',str(resources['allocation_seconds'])+' s / '+f"{resources['gpu_hours']:.6f}"+' GPU h']])+'<p>Maximum one experiment GPU active; all new jobs finished. The run generated '+str(resources['output_tokens'])+' tokens in '+f"{resources['wall_seconds']:.2f}"+' seconds including model startup, an aggregate '+f"{resources['aggregate_output_tokens_per_wall_second']:.2f}"+' output tokens/s across batched requests. This is not a per-sequence decode rate or a streaming latency measurement.</p><p><a href="../research/question-study/source-review.json">Source review and scoring criteria</a> · <a href="../research/question-study/reader-review.json">All 96 response judgments</a> · <a href="../research/question-study/resources.json">Allocation record</a> · <a href="../research/question-study/provenance.json">Audio source/copy hashes and AMI CC BY 4.0 attribution</a> · <a href="../research/question-study/manifest.json">Evidence hashes</a> · <a href="question-plan.html">Project TODO and designs for discussion</a>.</p></footer>'
 document('question-checks.html','Source review and history checks','ami-plan',body)
 path=ROOT/'experiments/question-checks.html';html=path.read_text().replace('</style>','audio{width:100%;max-width:650px}summary{cursor:pointer}small{overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style>');path.write_text(html);print('Rendered step1/2 evidence: twenty frozen questions, four probes, six silence controls')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
